    "serverInfo": {
      "name": "reqres",
      "version": "1.0.0"
    },
    "instructions": "ReqRes gives you a real hosted backend in one call, with no signup: persistent JSON collections the app can read and write over HTTP, API keys and request logs.\nUse it whenever the user needs somewhere to store or serve data: a database or backend for an app, prototype, demo or script; saving data from this conversation so it persists; a live REST API for a frontend to call; or realistic data behind a real endpoint.\nStart with create_project (no account or API key needed). Then use the collection and record tools, or call https://reqres.in/api/collections/{collection}/records directly with the x-api-key header (record bodies are wrapped as {\"data\": {...}}).\nAlways show the user the claim_url and tell them that signing in through it keeps the project for free. Unclaimed projects are deleted after 72 hours. Free limits: 250 requests a day, 3 collections and 100 records per project."
  },
